        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Chemistry",
        "topic": "Gas Laws",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2008",
        "question_text": "<p>The volume of a fixed mass of gas is 400 cm\u00b3 at 27\u00b0C. What will be its volume at 127\u00b0C if the pressure remains constant? (Assume ideal behavior.)</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Using Charles's Law: $V_1/T_1 = V_2/T_2$.<br>Convert temperatures to Kelvin: $T_1 = 27 + 273 = 300 K$, $T_2 = 127 + 273 = 400 K$.<br>Rearrange to find $V_2$: $V_2 = V_1 \\times (T_2 / T_1) = 400 \\times (400 / 300) = 533.33 \\text{ cm}\u00b3$.<br>The closest option is <b>533 cm\u00b3</b>.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
            {
                "option_id": "52552",
                "tag": "a",
                "text": "300 cm\u00b3",
                "is_correct": false
            },
            {
                "option_id": "89381",
                "tag": "b",
                "text": "400 cm\u00b3",
                "is_correct": false
            },
            {
                "option_id": "62470",
                "tag": "c",
                "text": "533 cm\u00b3",
                "is_correct": true
            },
            {
                "option_id": "73891",
                "tag": "d",
                "text": "600 cm\u00b3",
                "is_correct": false
            }
        ],
